## (d) Claude-format .claude/ dirs — DOCUMENTED (not run here; see note)
This worktree's harness hook rejects any bash command that touches `.claude/` (it guards the
worktree's own harness config), so the empirical home-`.claude/skills` test was not run in this
session. The authoritative answer is in opencode's own built-in "customize-opencode" skill, dumped
verbatim above by `opencode debug skill` (location <built-in>), which states the file-location
contract for 1.18.8:
  - External skills AUTO-LOADED from: `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and
    `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (HOME-level only; a PROJECT-local `.claude/skills` is NOT in
    the scan list). Toggle with env `OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_SKILLS=1` /
    `OPENCODE_DISABLE_EXTERNAL_SKILLS=1` (both present in the 1.18.8 binary string table).
  - There is NO `.claude/agents` entry anywhere in the file-locations table: opencode agents load
    only from `.opencode/agent(s)/` or `~/.config/opencode/agent(s)/` or the `agent` config key.
    So a raw Claude-format `.claude/agents/*.md` is NOT read as an opencode agent (matches desk
    recon) — it must be converted to opencode frontmatter, as demonstrated for soma-lead in (b).
Implication for a rebuild: claude-soma's skills can be dropped under `~/.claude/skills/` (or copied
to `.opencode/skill/`, proven in (a)); its `agents/*.md` must be converted (mechanical: rename
`permissionMode`->drop/`permission`, keep description, set `mode`, prefix `model` with a provider);
its `skills/*/SKILL.md` load as-is including the Claude `allowed-tools` frontmatter.
